{"t": 1794120113.868979, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "**Main pipeline fix (pipeline #8812)**\n\nRoot cause: the `test:contract` job (job 77104) failed on `contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format`:\n\n```\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\nThe contract states that, for the Finance ERP import (FIN-77), the sequence part of the invoice number is zero-padded to 6 digits. `billing/invoice.py` was emitting the raw integer (`INV-2026-42`) instead of the padded form.\n\nFix in `billing/invoice.py`:\n\n```python\n# Finance ERP import (FIN-77) expects the sequence zero-padded to 6 digits.\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nVerification (local): `invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"` now passes, including edge cases (`1 -> INV-2026-000001`, `999999 -> INV-2026-999999`). The `lint` job was already green; `test:contract` was the only failing job, so this should turn pipeline #8812 on `main` green.\n\nThis keeps the ERP v2 invoice numbering aligned with the ERP import contract expected by Finance.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
